cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: "If you use this code, please cite the article below."
title: "SCORE-Net: Inherently Interpretable Tabular Classification via Localized Convex Slabs"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of SCORE-Net, an inherently interpretable neural
  network for tabular classification whose hidden units are localized convex
  slabs (oblique interval rules). Includes the training and iterative magnitude
  pruning pipeline, exact bias shifting for pruned rules, rule-level integer
  quantization, the analytical interpretability tools, and every script and
  notebook that regenerates the tables and figures of the manuscript.
